---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import IndustryResources from '../../components/IndustryResources.astro';
import QuillajaSelection from '../../components/QuillajaSelection.astro';
import ApplicationTasks from '../../components/ApplicationTasks.astro';
---
<PageLayout title="Botanical Beverage Ingredients: Tea & Stevia Formulation" description="Evaluate tea bitterness and astringency, stevia bitter aftertaste and lingering sweetness. Connect beverage formulation trials with ingredient forms and samples." lang="en" heroTitle="Beverages" heroSubtitle="From application conditions to a purchasing specification">
<section id="plant-based-ingredients" class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl">
<h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold">Tea and botanical ingredients for plant-based drinks</h2>
<p class="mt-4 text-gray-700">In an oat-based drink, the oat base provides body while the tea ingredient contributes tea flavor and color. Our ingredient selection focuses on tea extracts, fruit-derived powders and botanical sweeteners; the plant-milk base and its emulsifier–stabilizer system are separate formulation choices.</p>
<p class="mt-4 text-gray-700">For a green tea oat latte, dissolve a soluble tea extract separately rather than treating it as leaf powder. Compare with a base-only control at the actual protein, salt and pH levels, then check sandy texture, sediment redispersibility and heat-induced flocculation after processing and storage. Goji juice powder follows a different route: a fruit-flavored drink mix, with carrier, reconstitution and color checks rather than a plant-milk base.</p>
<a class="inline-block mt-4 text-primary underline" href="/plant-extracts/ingredients/green-tea#formulation-oat-latte">Green tea oat latte: ingredient roles and trial sequence →</a>
</div></section>
<div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><p data-tea-family-discovery class="my-6"><a class="text-primary underline" href="/products/tea-extracts">Green, black and oolong tea: soluble powders and concentrate projects</a></p></div>
<section data-pomegranate-discovery class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold"><a class="underline text-primary" href="/resources/blog/pomegranate-flavour-selection">Pomegranate drinks: choose the flavour direction before deastringency</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-700">Separate fresh-fruit and cooked-fruit aroma, red colour and drying mouthfeel; total phenols cannot replace juice sampling.</p></div></section>
<QuillajaSelection lang="en" />
<ApplicationTasks lang="en" industry="beverages" />
<section class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl">
<p class="text-xl text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-10">Evaluate botanical ingredients in the actual beverage, not just in water. Clarity, taste and storage behavior depend on the complete formula and process.</p>
<h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold mb-6">Troubleshooting and validation</h2><div class="space-y-5">
<div class="p-6 bg-off-white rounded-xl"><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Haze or sediment</h3><p class="mt-2 text-gray-600">Compare dissolution and dispersion at your target pH, water hardness and use level. Check the influence of carrier, filtration and mixing order before changing the ingredient.</p></div>
<div id="tea-bitterness-astringency" class="p-6 bg-off-white rounded-xl"><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Tea bitterness, astringency and color drift</h3><p class="mt-2 text-gray-600">Record bitterness as a taste separately from astringency, the drying or puckering mouthfeel. Compare green tea extract samples and use levels in the same water, acid and sweetener system so a base change is not mistaken for a material difference. Recheck both sensory attributes and color after heat treatment and during storage in the intended package.</p><a class="inline-block mt-3 text-primary underline" href="/plant-extracts/ingredients/green-tea#formulation-citrus-tea">Green tea citrus trial: addition order and bitterness/astringency checks →</a></div>
<div class="p-6 bg-off-white rounded-xl"><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Process mismatch</h3><p class="mt-2 text-gray-600">Include pasteurization or hot-fill conditions in pilot trials. Assess shelf-life and microbial controls with your formulation and quality team.</p></div>
</div><div class="mt-10 p-8 bg-primary/5 rounded-xl"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">What to include in your brief</h2><p class="mt-3 text-gray-700">Beverage format, pH, process temperature/time, clarity target, use level and destination market.</p><p class="mt-3 text-gray-600">Also include the ingredient, first order quantity and documents needed. Grades, samples and documents are subject to availability; certification and regulatory suitability require product- and market-specific review. These are evaluation considerations, not a formulation or suitability guarantee.</p><a href="/request-quote?request=application&amp;source=beverages&amp;application=beverages" class="inline-block mt-5 px-6 py-3 bg-primary text-white rounded-lg">Discuss application requirements</a><a href="/resources/downloads" class="inline-block mt-5 ml-4 text-primary underline">Get the sourcing checklist</a></div>
</div></section>
<section data-citrus-research class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold"><a class="text-primary underline" href="/resources/blog/hesperidin-material-choice">Citrus flavonoids in water: hesperidin or glucosyl hesperidin?</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-600">Compare research on unmodified hesperidin, glucosyl hesperidin and protein-containing delivery systems. Separate material identity, dissolution requirements and destination-market conditions.</p></div></section>
<section data-hibiscus-research class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold"><a class="text-primary underline" href="/resources/blog/hibiscus-color-endpoints">Hibiscus color: appearance and pigment content are different endpoints</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-600">Research reading on roselle fruit drinks: separate color coordinates from monomeric anthocyanin measurements.</p></div></section>
<section data-citrus-bitterness-research class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold"><a class="text-primary underline" href="/resources/blog/citrus-delayed-bitterness">Why does citrus juice become bitter during storage?</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-600">Compare juice ingredients across the intended processing and evaluation timeline, separating limonin formation rate from later concentration.</p></div></section>
<section data-astaxanthin-research class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold"><a class="text-primary underline" href="/resources/blog/astaxanthin-beverage-stability">Astaxanthin drinks: interfaces for liquid and powder formats</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-600">Separate orange-red appearance, immediate drying retention and storage behavior when planning trials for the finished drink.</p></div></section>
<IndustryResources lang="en" industry="beverages" />
<section data-cocoa-discovery class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold"><a class="underline text-primary" href="/resources/blog/cocoa-selection">Cocoa powder or cocoa extract? Match chocolate character and flavanol delivery separately</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-700">Compare cocoa powder, flavanol-preserving powder and assayed extracts by chocolate character, composition and the finished formulation.</p></div></section>
<section data-ginger-discovery class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold"><a class="underline text-primary" href="/resources/blog/ginger-selection">Choosing processed ginger: why more shogaol does not settle the aroma question</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-700">Choose ginger by aroma and warming sensation separately, with study-specific drying, extraction and carrier evidence.</p></div></section>
<section data-beetroot-discovery class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold"><a class="underline text-primary" href="/resources/blog/beetroot-product-formats">Beetroot powder product development: what three Amazon listings reveal</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-700">Three seller-displayed beet products show different food, bulk-mixing and flavoured-drink briefs, without ranking efficacy or demand.</p></div></section>
<section data-botanical-comparison class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold"><a class="underline text-primary" href="/resources/blog/butterfly-pea-protein-beverages">Butterfly pea blue in protein drinks: choose the colour window before testing protein interactions</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-700">Butterfly pea colour depends on pH, temperature and the protein–sugar–mineral system. Read the binding evidence before planning a blue protein drink.</p></div></section>
<section data-botanical-comparison class="section-padding"><div class="container-wide max-w-4xl"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold"><a class="underline text-primary" href="/resources/blog/monk-fruit-specification-numbers">Buying monk fruit: how to read °Brix, mogroside V percentages and 1:1 sugar-replacement claims</a></h2><p class="mt-4 text-gray-700">Distinguish °Brix, mogroside V assays and sugar-replacement ratios using named specifications, four retail products and model-derived sweetness data.</p></div></section>
</PageLayout>
